I/O. Applies to subsequent sequential calls on that object.","representation":["FileSnapshotSink.closed == true"],"invalidators":[],"reinterpreters":[],"durability":"In-memory object state only.","recovery":"No persistent reconstruction of this flag is shown; retained directories do not encode terminal-call success.","source_ids":["file_snapshot.go:1:300","file_snapshot.go:397:500"],"unknowns":["No concurrent-call synchronization contract is established.","The flag alone cannot distinguish either terminal method's successful and failed outcomes."]},{"id":"file_snapshot_cancel_removal_completed","meaning":"On the first cancellation path, finalization and os.RemoveAll(s.dir) both returned successfully. This is distinct from a nil return through the already-closed branch.","identity":{"sink":"The FileSnapshotSink object executing its first Cancel path","artifact_path":"s.dir, initialized by Create to the store path plus snapshot name and .tmp"},"established_by":["file_snapshot_cancel_first"],"consumed_by":[],"validity_context":"Established only at successful completion of removal after successful finalization. It records that operation's outcome, not permanent absence under subsequent filesystem activity.","representation":["Control flow reaches os.RemoveAll(s.dir) and it returns nil."],"invalidators":[],"reinterpreters":[],"durability":"Filesystem removal completed according to the API return; cancellation does not sync the parent directory.","recovery":"Crash recovery of removed or residual artifacts is not established. Listing independently skips .tmp directories.","source_ids":["file_snapshot.go:1:300","file_snapshot.go:397:500"],"unknowns":["No actual consumer of this branch-specific completion assertion has been inspected.","Directory-name uniqueness, concurrent path reuse and persistence across crash are not established."]}],"surfaces":[{"entry_point":"Raft.takeSnapshot / compactLogsWithTrailing / removeOldLogs","disposition":"mapped","behavior_ids":["B_snapshot_orchestration","B_log_compaction"],"reason":"Snapshot orchestration and deletion bounds are visible; capture establishment and adapter contracts remain open.","source_ids":["snapshot.go:125:278"],"high_consequence":true},{"entry_point":"FileSnapshotSink.Close","disposition":"mapped","behavior_ids":["B_file_snapshot_close"],"reason":"First-close and repeated-close paths are distinguished; metadata and retention callees remain unread.","source_ids":["file_snapshot.go:397:500"],"high_consequence":true},{"entry_point":"FileSnapshotSink.Cancel","disposition":"mapped","behavior_ids":["file_snapshot_cancel_first","file_snapshot_cancel_already_closed","file_snapshot_close_terminal_path"],"reason":"The supplied implementation resolves first-call cleanup, finalization failure, removal failure and already-closed cancellation. The directly connected Close path explains how the shared flag can suppress cancellation after failure or publication. Creation and listing establish the temporary-path context. Mapping records this behavior without asserting cleanup or recovery correctness.","source_ids":["file_snapshot.go:1:300","file_snapshot.go:350:396","file_snapshot.go:397:500","file_snapshot.go:501:551","snapshot.go:1:100"],"high_consequence":true}]},"directed_question":null,"parameters":{},"materials":[{"id":"fsm.go:1:80","file":"fsm.go","start_line":1,"end_line":80,"kind":"interface_statement","text":"// Copyright (c) HashiCorp, Inc.\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0\n\npackage raft\n\nimport (\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"io\"\n\t\"time\"\n\n\thclog \"github.com/hashicorp/go-hclog\"\n\t\"github.com/hashicorp/go-metrics/compat\"\n)\n\n// FSM is implemented by clients to make use of the replicated log.\ntype FSM interface {\n\t// Apply is called once a log entry is committed by a majority of the cluster.\n\t//\n\t// Apply should apply the log to the FSM. Apply must be deterministic and\n\t// produce the same result on all peers in the cluster.\n\t//\n\t// The returned value is returned to the client as the ApplyFuture.Response.\n\tApply(*Log) interface{}\n\n\t// Snapshot returns an FSMSnapshot used to: support log compaction, to\n\t// restore the FSM to a previous state, or to bring out-of-date followers up\n\t// to a recent log index.\n\t//\n\t// The Snapshot implementation should return quickly, because Apply can not\n\t// be called while Snapshot is running. Generally this means Snapshot should\n\t// only capture a pointer to the state, and any expensive IO should happen\n\t// as part of FSMSnapshot.Persist.\n\t//\n\t// Apply and Snapshot are always called from the same thread, but Apply will\n\t// be called concurrently with FSMSnapshot.Persist. This means the FSM should\n\t// be implemented to allow for concurrent updates while a snapshot is happening.\n\t//\n\t// Clients of this library should make no assumptions about whether a returned\n\t// Snapshot() will actually be stored by Raft. In fact it's quite possible that\n\t// any Snapshot returned by this call will be discarded, and that\n\t// FSMSnapshot.Persist will never be called. Raft will always call\n\t// FSMSnapshot.Release however.\n\tSnapshot() (FSMSnapshot, error)\n\n\t// Restore is used to restore an FSM from a snapshot. It is not called\n\t// concurrently with any other command. The FSM must discard all previous\n\t// state before restoring the snapshot.\n\tRestore(snapshot io.ReadCloser) error\n}\n\n// BatchingFSM extends the FSM interface to add an ApplyBatch function. This can\n// optionally be implemented by clients to enable multiple logs to be applied to\n// the FSM in batches. Up to MaxAppendEntries could be sent in a batch.\ntype BatchingFSM interface {\n\t// ApplyBatch is invoked once a batch of log entries has been committed and\n\t// are ready to be applied to the FSM. ApplyBatch will take in an array of\n\t// log entries. These log entries will be in the order they were committed,\n\t// will not have gaps, and could be of a few log types. Clients should check\n\t// the log type prior to attempting to decode the data attached. Presently\n\t// the LogCommand and LogConfiguration types will be sent.\n\t//\n\t// The returned slice must be the same length as the input and each response\n\t// should correlate to the log at the same index of the input. The returned\n\t// values will be made available in the ApplyFuture returned by Raft.Apply\n\t// method if that method was called on the same Raft node as the FSM.\n\tApplyBatch([]*Log) []interface{}\n\n\tFSM\n}\n\n// FSMSnapshot is returned by an FSM in response to a Snapshot\n// It must be safe to invoke FSMSnapshot methods with concurrent\n// calls to Apply.\ntype FSMSnapshot interface {\n\t// Persist should dump all necessary state to the WriteCloser 'sink',\n\t// and call sink.Close() when finished or call sink.Cancel() on error.\n\tPersist(sink SnapshotSink) error\n\n\t// Release is invoked when we are finished with the snapshot.\n\tRelease()","content_digest":"56b93e1edbbd11b74d1fdc3a1e45a25facdb45b91495b98a25efe45abc83a869"},{"id":"snapshot.go:125:278","file":"snapshot.go","start_line":125,"end_line":278,"kind":"code_observation","content_digest":"45d46961871682958b155bd719bf025ff7e3a31ec948e21c8f6b9447d026cb3d","source_view_id":"source-view-3"},{"id":"file_snapshot.go:397:500","file":"file_snapshot.go","start_line":397,"end_line":500,"kind":"code_observation","text":"func (s *FileSnapshotSink) Close() error {\n\t// Make sure close is idempotent\n\tif s.closed {\n\t\treturn nil\n\t}\n\ts.closed = true\n\n\t// Close the open handles\n\tif err := s.finalize(); err != nil {\n\t\ts.logger.Error(\"failed to finalize snapshot\", \"error\", err)\n\t\tif delErr := os.RemoveAll(s.dir); delErr != nil {\n\t\t\ts.logger.Error(\"failed to delete temporary snapshot directory\", \"path\", s.dir, \"error\", delErr)\n\t\t\treturn delErr\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn err\n\t}\n\n\t// Write out the meta data\n\tif err := s.writeMeta(); err != nil {\n\t\ts.logger.Error(\"failed to write metadata\", \"error\", err)\n\t\treturn err\n\t}\n\n\t// Move the directory into place\n\tnewPath := strings.TrimSuffix(s.dir, tmpSuffix)\n\tif err := os.Rename(s.dir, newPath); err != nil {\n\t\ts.logger.Error(\"failed to move snapshot into place\", \"error\", err)\n\t\treturn err\n\t}\n\n\tif !s.noSync && runtime.GOOS != \"windows\" { // skipping fsync for directory entry edits on Windows, only needed for *nix style file systems\n\t\tparentFH, err := os.Open(s.parentDir)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\ts.logger.Error(\"failed to open snapshot parent directory\", \"path\", s.parentDir, \"error\", err)\n\t\t\treturn err\n\t\t}\n\t\tdefer parentFH.Close()\n\n\t\tif err = parentFH.Sync(); err != nil {\n\t\t\ts.logger.Error(\"failed syncing parent directory\", \"path\", s.parentDir, \"error\", err)\n\t\t\treturn err\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n\t// Reap any old snapshots\n\tif err := s.store.ReapSnapshots(); err != nil {\n\t\treturn err\n\t}\n\n\treturn nil\n}\n\n// Cancel is used to indicate an unsuccessful end.\nfunc (s *FileSnapshotSink) Cancel() error {\n\t// Make sure close is idempotent\n\tif s.closed {\n\t\treturn nil\n\t}\n\ts.closed = true\n\n\t// Close the open handles\n\tif err := s.finalize(); err != nil {\n\t\ts.logger.Error(\"failed to finalize snapshot\", \"error\", err)\n\t\treturn err\n\t}\n\n\t// Attempt to remove all artifacts\n\treturn os.RemoveAll(s.dir)\n}\n\n// finalize is used to close all of our resources.\nfunc (s *FileSnapshotSink) finalize() error {\n\t// Flush any remaining data\n\tif err := s.buffered.Flush(); err != nil {\n\t\treturn err\n\t}\n\n\t// Sync to force fsync to disk\n\tif !s.noSync {\n\t\tif err := s.stateFile.Sync(); err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn err\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n\t// Get the file size\n\tstat, statErr := s.stateFile.Stat()\n\n\t// Close the file\n\tif err := s.stateFile.Close(); err != nil {\n\t\treturn err\n\t}\n\n\t// Set the file size, check after we close\n\tif statErr != nil {\n\t\treturn statErr\n\t}\n\ts.meta.Size = stat.Size()\n\n\t// Set the CRC\n\ts.meta.CRC = s.stateHash.Sum(nil)\n\treturn nil\n}\n\n// writeMeta is used to write out the metadata we have.","content_digest":"72b15cc6a6078db49350bfd2a0407f914ffd4eca1a1790d155f4427f34b51b4f"},{"id":"snapshot.go:1:278","file":"snapshot.go","start_line":1,"end_line":278,"kind":"interface_statement","content_digest":"45d46961871682958b155bd719bf025ff7e3a31ec948e21c8f6b9447d026cb3d","source_view_id":"source-view-3"}],"required_material_ids":["file_snapshot.go:397:500","fsm.go:1:80","snapshot.go:125:278","snapshot.go:1:278"],"projection_level":0,"source_rule":"Orientation, provenance IDs and declaration hints are navigation, not source evidence. Only attached exact source supports current implementation judgments.","selected_question":{"disposition":null,"preferred_check":"source_review","requests":[{"file":"snapshot.go","start_line":1,"end_line":278,"reason":"Acquire snapshot interfaces and the complete takeSnapshot and compaction control flow to establish terminal-call semantics, error propagation and the exact reclamation consumer."},{"file":"fsm.go","start_line":1,"end_line":80,"reason":"Acquire the FSM snapshot persistence contract, especially sink ownership and required handling of Close or Cancel outcomes."},{"file":"file_snapshot.go","start_line":397,"end_line":500,"reason":"Inspect Close and Cancel declarations and terminal branches, including the closed latch, publication steps, returned errors and repeated-call results."}],"question":"For the principal fact F_snapshot_close_accepted, does takeSnapshot's consumption of successful Persist and subsequent Close returns justify recording snapshot metadata and requesting log compaction when an earlier terminal call on the same FileSnapshotSink failed or cancelled publication, or does the applicable Persist/sink contract exclude that history?","importance":"If this acceptance permits reclamation without usable replacement recovery evidence, restart or replica recovery could lose required history. The immediate question concerns snapshot acceptance consumed by metadata update and compaction; legal reachability and actual recovery loss remain unestablished.","source_ids":["file_snapshot.go:397:500","snapshot.go:125:278"],"participants":["takeSnapshot caller","Application FSMSnapshot implementation","FileSnapshotSink"],"objects":["Snapshot sink object","Published snapshot","Snapshot progress metadata","Log interval eligible for compaction"],"contexts":["Built-in file snapshot store when selected","Sequential terminal calls on the same sink","Snapshot persistence and publication errors"],"event_paths":["takeSnapshot -> FSMSnapshot.Persist -> sink terminal call -> takeSnapshot Close -> snapshot metadata update and compaction"],"activity_classes":["A6"],"behavior_ids":["B_snapshot_orchestration","B_file_snapshot_close","file_snapshot_close_terminal_path","file_snapshot_cancel_first","file_snapshot_cancel_already_closed","B_log_compaction"],"fact_ids":["F_snapshot_close_accepted"],"obligation_relation_kind":"consumption","counterevidence":["takeSnapshot returns before metadata update and compaction if Persist or its subsequent Close returns an error; propagation of an earlier terminal error may therefore exclude the suspected history.","The first Close success path performs finalization, metadata writing, rename, conditional parent synchronization and retention before returning nil. This provides a publication mechanism distinct from the already-closed return.","compactLogsWithTrailing bounds deletion by both the snapshot index and the trailing-log setting and can skip deletion entirely; reaching compaction does not itself establish history loss.","Correct terminal-call ownership or an applicable Persist contract may exclude returning nil after failed or cancelled publication; those contracts are not supplied."],"unknowns":["The applicable SnapshotSink and FSMSnapshot.Persist contracts, including terminal-call ownership and error propagation.","Whether a permitted Persist execution can return nil after an unsuccessful or cancelling terminal call.","Whether the applicable contract permits the already-closed nil return to be consumed as successful publication; the implementation returns nil without preserving an earlier terminal error.","Whether a legally reachable acceptance without usable publication leads to deletion of history required for recovery under the actual retained snapshots and trailing-log configuration.","Whether any candidate local contract applies independently of unspecified application behavior.","The actual selected snapshot-store and filesystem configuration."],"priority":1,"trigger_rationale":"F_snapshot_close_accepted is the sole principal fact and consumption is the selected lifecycle. Its producer, takeSnapshot, immediately uses the accepted returns to update snapshot metadata and request compaction. Supporting sink behaviors show that a first terminal call sets closed before fallible I/O and subsequent sequential Close calls return nil without publication work. These observations establish the discriminator, not a contract violation. Interface source is still needed to determine whether the triggering Persist history is permitted. Recovery remains a potential consequence rather than a second activity context or checked responsibility."},"source_receipt":{"id":"cef4ba016b8d48d189d36dfe8619139a","snapshot_id":"2fa76ee677a049049ceb65e2b0dddf3b","purpose":"depth","status":"complete","items":[{"request":{"file":"snapshot.go","start_line":1,"end_line":278,"reason":"Acquire snapshot interfaces and the complete takeSnapshot and compaction control flow to establish terminal-call semantics, error propagation and the exact reclamation consumer."},"status":"acquired","material_ids":["snapshot.go:1:278"],"new_chars":665,"new_chunks":0,"reason":"","file_metadata":{"file":"snapshot.go","lines":278,"content_digest":"45d46961871682958b155bd719bf025ff7e3a31ec948e21c8f6b9447d026cb3d","snapshot_id":"2fa76ee677a049049ceb65e2b0dddf3b","encoding":"u